+The Verification Engine does not create the authoritative commit receipt. The
+World Kernel MUST atomically make visible all three of the following, or none:
+
+1. the resulting authoritative World version;
+2. the immutable `WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT`; and
+3. the durable committed-event delivery intent.
+
+The delivery intent is not an outcome event and does not prove delivery.
+`VerificationReceipt` is a pre-commit verification artifact bound to one
+parent/candidate/evidence/policy context. It is distinct from the immutable
+`WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT`, which exists only after a successful World Kernel CAS
+commit. Verification, event persistence, or Chronicle projection alone MUST
+NOT be presented as proof of World commitment.
 
